course: dictionary
lesson: 4860
title: Medicines and safety
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ibuprofen is a medicine. It helps with pain, fever and swelling, so it is often used for headaches, toothache and sprains. Medicines can help us feel better, but they can also cause harm if they are used the wrong way.
explain: Only an adult should give you ibuprofen, at the right dose for your age and weight. Never take medicine from someone else's packet. «Children's ibuprofen» is made for children, but the dose still matters.
explain: Sometimes a medicine is not right for an illness. «Ibuprofen should not be given for chickenpox unless a doctor says so.» When you are unsure, always ask an adult or a doctor before you take anything.
fact: Ibuprofen is a medicine that reduces pain, fever and swelling.
fact: Ibuprofen is sold as tablets or liquid, under names like Nurofen or Advil.
fact: Doctors usually suggest paracetamol or ibuprofen first, and switch to the other only if the first hasn't helped.
fact: «Aspirin is not given to children under 16.»
fact: A medicine must always be given at the right dose for age and weight.
exercise: What is ibuprofen? | *A common medicine that reduces pain, fever and swelling | A type of sports shoe | A drink for cold days | A kind of sweet
exercise: «Paracetamol and ibuprofen are both safe for most children at the right dose.» What must be right for them to be safe? | The shop where they were bought | The colour of the packet | *The dose | The time of day
exercise: Who should give you ibuprofen? | Any friend at school | A stranger in the park | *An adult | Anyone who has a spare packet
test: Why must you never take medicine from someone else's packet? | Packets are too heavy to carry | It might taste nice | *It might not be the right medicine or dose for you | It makes the tablets go out of date
test: «Ibuprofen should not be given for chickenpox unless a doctor says so.» What does this tell you? | Ibuprofen is always the best medicine | Chickenpox is cured by ibuprofen | Doctors never give medicines to children | *Doctors decide when ibuprofen is right for an illness
exam: If you have a headache and feel unsure about medicine, what is the safest thing to do? | Guess the right dose and take it | *Ask an adult or a doctor before you take anything | Take a tablet from your friend's bag | Take two tablets to be sure
